.TH "mlaunch" "1" "2026-10-13" "mlaunch @VERSION@" "mlaunch manual"
.SH NAME
mlaunch \- minimal app-only launcher client for the mango Wayland compositor
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmlaunch\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.br
\fBmlaunch\fR \-\-help | \-h
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBmlaunch\fR connects to a running \fBmango\fR(1) compositor and opens a
small centered layer-shell overlay with an exclusive keyboard grab. It
searches applications only — no file or run modes:
.IP \(bu
desktop applications from every \fIapplications\fR dir on the XDG data path
(Nix profile paths and the Flatpak export dirs are appended defensively)
.IP \(bu
AppImages found under \fI$HOME/Applications\fR (direct exec when the bit is
set, \fBappimage-run\fR fallback otherwise)
.IP \(bu
running windows with no matching application, focused via foreign-toplevel
activation; apps with live windows carry a running dot
.PP
Each row shows the app icon (XDG icon-theme lookup, fallback glyph), the
name, the \fIComment\fR/\fIGenericName\fR line, and the running dot.
Filtering is a fuzzy subsequence match over the name, description and Exec
basename.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-font\fR \fI<pango font>\fR
Font description, default \fIsans 10\fR.
.TP
\fB\-w\fR, \fB\-\-width\fR \fI<px>\fR
Logical overlay width, default \fI440\fR.
.TP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-rows\fR \fI<n>\fR
Maximum visible rows, default \fI8\fR.
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<name>\fR
Show on the named output instead of the first one.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show help.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBMLAUNCH_FONT\fR, \fBMLAUNCH_WIDTH\fR, \fBMLAUNCH_MAX_ROWS\fR,
\fBMLAUNCH_ICON_THEME\fR, \fBMLAUNCH_APPIMAGE_DIRS\fR, \fBMLAUNCH_OUTPUT\fR
The same knobs as the flags above (flags win).
.SH KEYS
.IP \(bu
Type to filter; \fBUp\fR/\fBDown\fR or \fBTab\fR to change selection
.IP \(bu
\fBEnter\fR launch the selected app
.IP \(bu
\fBEscape\fR close
.IP \(bu
\fBCtrl+W\fR delete word, \fBCtrl+U\fR clear the line
.PP
The mouse selects, launches and scrolls.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBmango\fR(1), \fBmmsg\fR(1), \fBmangonag\fR(1)
